<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a vibratory conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A vibratory conveyor moves material through controlled vibration instead of belts, chains, or rollers. Electromagnetic, electromechanical, or pneumatic drives generate oscillations that propel bulk solids in micro-hops along a trough. No belt, chain, or rollers contact the product, making vibratory conveyors ideal for sanitary and gentle-handling applications.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">Vibratory conveyor vs. vibratory feeder?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A conveyor transports material over distance. A feeder meters material at a controlled rate from a hopper or bin. Feeders prioritize rate accuracy. Conveyors prioritize throughput and distance. Many systems combine both: a feeder meters from storage, and a conveyor transports to the next process.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What is a vibratory bowl feeder?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A round vibratory device with a helical track inside. Parts dump into the bowl, vibration drives them up the track, and tooling along the track rejects misoriented parts. Correctly oriented parts exit single-file to the downstream machine. Essential for automated assembly of caps, fasteners, and electronic components.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What materials can vibratory conveyors handle?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Most dry bulk solids: powders, granules, pellets, flakes, crystals, and small parts. Food ingredients, chemicals, pharmaceuticals, metal parts, and recyclables. Very sticky, wet, or highly cohesive materials may require specialized trough coatings or higher-amplitude drives.</p>

</div>
